REMIX:  PIXEL PORK RINDS — “SORRY, UNCLE BOB” EDITION

STYLE / LOOK

Same grimy Midwest diner aesthetic as the original: tungsten lights, dusty blinds, shallow DOF, cinematic grain.
REplace the main character with The Pig, who is @artexmg.djsnoutspi
Humans react with dramatic tension, shock, and fear — meme exaggeration.

Keep everything friendly, comedic, and surreal.

SCENE SCRIPT (SHOT BY SHOT)
0.0–1.5s — Establishing Shot

Wide shot of a diner booth.
Instead of a man, @artexmg.djsnoutspi sits upright, holding a bag of PIXEL PORK RINDS with tiny yarn hooves.

Cinematic grain. Soft camera pan-in.
People in the background stare in awkward silence.

A waitress passes by and murmurs (deadpan):
“You… uh… gonna order, or… is this… enough?”

1.5–3.0s — Close-Up on the Yarn Pig

@artexmg.djsnoutspi squints, opens the bag with surprising determination.

Sound: CRINKLE-CRUNCH of the bag (slightly too aggressive).

Pig quietly mutters:
“…Sorry, Uncle Bob.”

3.0–5.0s — Reaction Shot #1

Cut to a tough biker guy in a denim vest.
He freezes mid-chew.

Shock. Horror. Existential crisis.

“DUDE— DON’T DO IT!”

5.0–7.0s — Reaction Shot #2

Another man slowly turns, eyes wide.
Soft whisper:

“He knows… what he is.”

7.0–10.0s — CRUNCH MOMENT (Hero Shot)

Extreme macro close-up of @artexmg.djsnoutspi lifting a pork rind.
The seasoning flakes glisten like danger.

Slow motion as he bites down.
MEGA-CRUNCH (absurdly loud).

Everyone in the diner gasps.
One guy drops his coffee.

10.0–13.0s — Power Stare

pork rind slowly looks at the camera, still chewing.

A single eyebrow (stitched yarn) raises.

He whispers:
“Bob would’ve wanted this.”

13.0–15.0s — END CARD
A framed photo of “Uncle Bob the Pig” on the diner wall

A pork rind drops dramatically.

Text fades in with 1970s commercial punch:

WHEN YOUR SNACK IS YOUR UNCLE BOB

